  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin market cap rose 2.1% over 30D:</strong> Stablecoin market cap at $304.28B (2.1% higher over 30D) implies fresh dry powder entering crypto rails\u2014usually a constructive backdrop for settlement, trading, and on-chain cash demand. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/stablecoins-us-dollar-dominance-treasury-demand-boe?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stablecoin growth could boost dollar dominance, US Treasury demand: BoE official</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/15/circle-debuts-arc-blockchain-which-jeremy-allaire-calls-more-consequential-than-usdc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Circle debuts Arc blockchain which Jeremy Allaire calls \u2018more consequential\u2019 than USDC</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Bank rails are pushing stablecoins into treasury workflows:</strong> That pushes demand toward treasury and settlement use cases, not only exchange trading liquidity. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/16/deutsche-bank-nears-crypto-custody-service-debut-for-institutional-clients\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Deutsche Bank close to debuting crypto custody for institutions</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p